+## 2026-10-26 — Approved compact SK reconstruction, Phase 1 (implementation complete; review pending)
+
+- Implemented degree-contiguous six-component strain coefficient rows, combining
+  spheroidal/toroidal families before angular synthesis and rotating summed
+  point strains once. Existing shared strain formulas, physical orders, radial
+  traces and public full-field sampling are retained.
+- Reused exact radial interpolation, point geometry, order phases and Wigner
+  tables across active frequency bins under a shared 32 MiB cache-admission
+  budget; oversized entries use bounded chunk/per-call recomputation. This is
+  not a cap on total working memory.
+- The kernel route samples compact strain-only fields in 4096-point blocks,
+  computes receiver displacement once per frequency, and avoids displacement
+  and r-scaled strain work at integration points. The existing solve route is
+  unchanged.
+- Focused Release target builds with one job; 13/13 field/kernel tests pass
+  with one numerical thread, including compact/full component parity and forced
+  cache-full fallback. `git diff --check` passes. Expanded frozen field,
+  contact, plane, performance and Born validation plus independent Luna High
+  and Sol High reviews remain parent gates. No commit or push was made.
